    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d497-a1">

                <pb facs="0679" n="571" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg571"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tracy to Mr.
                            Wharton</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Navy Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-06-19"><hi rendition="#italic">June 19,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    copy of the instructions which have been issued by the Navy Department, in
                    pursuance of the proclamation of the President of June 15, 1891, containing a
                        <hi rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi>, with a view to their exchange,
                    should it he deemed desirable, for a copy of such instructions as may be issued
                    by the British Government on the same subject.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">B. F. Tracy</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of the Navy</hi>.</signed></closer>




